<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Clinical development principles">
  <div><strong>Research is not care</strong><span>A study answers a research question. It does not replace diagnosis or treatment.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Study type matters</strong><span>Observational and interventional studies answer different questions and carry different requirements.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Authorization has limits</strong><span>A Natural Product Number covers labelled use. It does not prove every proposed clinical application.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__feature">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Why clinical development</p>
    <h2>Mechanism is a starting point, not a clinical claim</h2>
    <p>Hydration physiology helps explain why fluid, electrolytes and glucose matter. Showing that a specific product improves a clinical outcome requires product-specific evidence in the population and setting being discussed.</p>
    <p>That is the purpose of clinical development: define the question, choose the right study and expand claims only when the evidence and regulatory basis support them.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Development pathway</p>
  <h2>From question to evidence</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__steps">
    <article class="bhd-page__step"><h3>Define the problem</h3><p>Specify the population, setting, hydration concern and outcome that matters.</p></article>
    <article class="bhd-page__step"><h3>Test feasibility</h3><p>Confirm that recruitment, preparation, measurements and workflow are practical before a larger study.</p></article>
    <article class="bhd-page__step"><h3>Write the protocol first</h3><p>Predefine the intervention, comparator where appropriate, outcomes, safety monitoring and analysis.</p></article>
    <article class="bhd-page__step"><h3>Get the required approvals</h3><p>Human research may require Research Ethics Board review and, for applicable natural health product trials, Health Canada authorization.</p></article>
    <article class="bhd-page__step"><h3>Report what was actually shown</h3><p>Keep conclusions within the studied formulation, dose, population and care context.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Research, care and regulation</p>
    <h2>Keep the boundaries clear</h2>
    <p>Clinical care is organized around an individual patient. Research follows a protocol designed to produce generalizable knowledge. Participation in a study should not be presented as a treatment recommendation.</p>
    <p>Health Canada identifies licensed natural health products with an eight-digit Natural Product Number. That authorization applies to labelled conditions of use. A clinical trial can ask a different question and may require a separate authorization pathway.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Regulatory distinction</span>
    <h3>NPN ≠ proof of every clinical use.</h3>
    <p>Product licensing, research ethics, trial authorization and evidence for a specific clinical claim are distinct.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Where the work lives</p>
  <h2>Three parts of the clinical program</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--3">
    <article><h3>Clinical Program</h3><p>Research questions, governance and the evidence needed to move forward.</p><a href="/pages/clinical-program">Clinical Program →</a></article>
    <article><h3>Pilot Studies</h3><p>Early studies that test measurements, workflows and feasibility before larger conclusions.</p><a href="/pages/pilot-studies">Pilot Studies →</a></article>
    <article><h3>Healthcare Applications</h3><p>Healthcare settings where hydration may matter, framed as questions rather than broad treatment claims.</p><a href="/pages/healthcare-applications">Healthcare Applications →</a></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__feature">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Ethics & transparency</p>
    <h2>Plan the study before celebrating the result</h2>
    <p>Consent in human research should be free, informed and ongoing. Applicable regulated trials should also be registered and their results disclosed in line with current requirements.</p>
    <p>Best Hydrate will name project-specific approvals only when they are verified and appropriate for public disclosure.</p>
  </div>
</section>

